<title>SOUTH AFRICA: BRENMIL HALF YEAR SHARE DIPS ON MAIZE PRICE.</title>
<headline>BRENMIL HALF YEAR SHARE DIPS ON MAIZE PRICE.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     6.2	   vs 11.3</p>
<p>    Operating profit	1.73	  vs 4.38</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.24	  vs 4.11</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.78	  vs 1.47</p>
<p>    Interest		  0.51 gain   vs 0.27 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  66.46	 vs 63.48</p>
<p>Full name: Brenner Mills Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South African maize miller Brenmil said that a rise in</p>
<p>the price of maize due to a crop shortage had pressurised its</p>
<p>margins. Lost production and sales due to industrial action also</p>
<p>hit profit.</p>
<p>The group said the current maize crop had been satisfactory</p>
<p>and prices had come down. This would see earnings improve in the</p>
<p>second half, but the full year figures are not expected to equal</p>
<p>those of last year, the firm said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
